The bloom computation iterates over all logs in a block. The number of logs is bounded by gas costs (each LOG opcode costs gas). The bloom computation is O(n) in the number of log entries and topics, where n is bounded by gas_limit/log_gas_cost. This is a known design characteristic.

## ITEM 8: CHK-0026 (PROP-W7B16-46)
Title: "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity: Is bloom keccak256 call count bounded?"
Severity: Low, Bug class: Resource Consumption

Similar to above - keccak256 calls during bloom are bounded by gas: each log entry produces (1 + num_topics) keccak256 calls, and each log costs gas. Total keccak256 calls <= block_gas_limit / min_log_gas * (1 + max_topics). This is bounded by design.

