## ITEM 16: CHK-0034 (PROP-0001)
Title: "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity: Is trie root computation deterministic regardless of insertion order?"
Severity: Critical

The trie root computation in reth uses `HashBuilder` from `alloy_trie`. The `HashBuilder::add_leaf()` and `add_branch()` methods expect keys to be inserted in sorted order (ascending nibble order). The `TrieNodeIter` walks the trie in sorted order by key. The MPT structure is deterministic by definition - same set of key-value pairs always produces the same root hash. Reth's trie iterates hashed keys in sorted order, and the HashBuilder produces canonical trie structure.

Code from crates/trie/trie/src/trie.rs:
```rust
